# Architecture

## 1) System Concept

A serial-driven microcontroller cluster (7 MCUs) where:

- user types commands on Serial Monitor with master node
- master node schedules distributed tasks
- worker nodes execute tasks on sensor/model data
- master aggregates and prints results live

## 2) Node Roles (7-node version)

- Node 0: Master + CLI
    - USB Serial interface to user
    - command parser + scheduler + aggregator
- Node 1–6: Workers
    - execute assigned tasks
    - run sensor processing / tiny inference

## 3) Network / Bus

- CAN bus for inter-node comms (recommended)
    - robust, multi-node friendly, easy fault demo
- Two 120Ω terminations at physical ends
- Shared GND across nodes

## 4) Hardware Blocks per Node

- MCU (same type on all nodes)
- CAN transceiver
- status LED
- debug/programming header
- optional local sensor connector

Master adds:

- USB-UART (or native USB) to PC Serial Monitor

## 5) Software Architecture

### Master firmware

1. CLI Layer
    - reads user command lines via serial
2. Command Parser
    - validates syntax/params
3. Task Scheduler
    - assigns task IDs and target workers
4. Node Manager
    - heartbeat tracking, online/offline state
5. CAN Transport
    - send commands, receive results
6. Aggregator
    - combines worker outputs
7. Reporter
    - prints progress, results, summaries

### Worker firmware

1. heartbeat tx
2. task rx handler
3. task executor (sensor/TinyML/self-test)
4. result tx
5. error/timeout handling

## 6) Serial Command Interface (core feature)

Supported commands:

- `help`
- `nodes`
- `status`
- `run <task> <node|all> <k=v ...>`
- `bench <task> <iters>`
- `stop <task_id>`
- `log <on|off>`

Examples:

- `run sensor_snapshot all`
- `run classify_sound 2 window=500`
- `bench imu_anomaly 30`
- `stop 1042`

## 7) Distributed Task Flow

1. User enters command on Serial Monitor
2. Master parses and creates `task_id`
3. Master dispatches over CAN
4. Workers execute and return results
5. Master prints:
    - per-node result lines
    - final summary
    - timeout/failure notices if any node fails

## 8) Message Types (protocol)

- `HEARTBEAT`
- `TASK_ASSIGN`
- `TASK_ACK`
- `TASK_RESULT`
- `TASK_PROGRESS` (optional)
- `TASK_STOP`
- `ERROR`

Key fields:

- `msg_type, task_id, src, dst, task_code, seq, payload`

## 9) Demo Tasks (good for school)

- `ping` (latency test)
- `self_test` (node health)
- `sensor_snapshot` (raw sensor read)
- `imu_anomaly` (simple threshold/feature model)
- `classify_sound` (tiny keyword/event model)
- `temp_trend` (windowed trend classification)

## 10) Serial Output Format (clean + judge-friendly)

- `OK task_id=1042 dispatched=6`
- `PROGRESS task_id=1042 done=3/6`
- `RESULT task_id=1042 node=3 label=normal score=0.88 latency_ms=34`
- `SUMMARY task_id=1042 majority=normal avg_latency_ms=39`
- `ERR task_id=1042 node=5 timeout`

## 11) Fault Tolerance (important scoring point)

- heartbeat every 500–1000 ms
- offline after N missed heartbeats
- scheduler skips offline nodes
- partial-result completion if one worker fails

## 12) Build Plan

- Phase 1: 2 nodes (master + 1 worker), CLI + ping
- Phase 2: 4 nodes, run/stop/status + heartbeat
- Phase 3: add 1–2 real sensor tasks
- Phase 4: scale to 6–8 nodes + benchmark mode
- Phase 5: finalize custom PCB and presentation metrics
